<section class="pf-section" id="institutional"><div class="wrap"><div class="pf-head"><div class="eyebrow">B. Most Institutionally Powerful</div><h2>AUTHORITY, NOT FAME.</h2><p>Prioritised by verified office, durable institutional position and documented capacity to make or shape decisions.</p></div><div id="pf-institutional" class="pf-grid"></div></div></section>
<section class="pf-section" id="capital"><div class="wrap"><div class="pf-head"><div class="eyebrow">C. Capital Controllers</div><h2>WHO CAN DIRECT DEPLOYABLE CAPITAL?</h2><p>Profiles with documented access to sovereign funds, voting control, family holdings, banking, custody, investment or major capital allocation.</p></div><div id="pf-capital" class="pf-grid"></div></div></section>
<section class="pf-section" id="connectors"><div class="wrap"><div class="pf-head"><div class="eyebrow">D. Network Connectors</div><h2>THE PEOPLE WHO BRIDGE SYSTEMS.</h2><p>Ranked by distinct documented access mechanisms, cross-system score and the number of institutional layers reached.</p></div><div id="pf-connectors" class="pf-grid"></div></div></section>
<section class="pf-section" id="gatekeepers"><div class="wrap"><div class="pf-head"><div class="eyebrow">E. Gatekeepers</div><h2>ACCESS IS OFTEN CONTROLLED BY THE LESS VISIBLE.</h2><p>Trustees, chairs, advisers, investment executives, institutional officers and durable intermediaries whose roles may be more operational than the public family name.</p></div><div id="pf-gatekeepers" class="pf-grid"></div></div></section>
<section class="pf-section" id="successors"><div class="wrap"><div class="pf-head"><div class="eyebrow">F. Succession Watch</div><h2>WHO MAY INHERIT OR ASSUME THE MECHANISM?</h2><p>Only publicly active adults with a documented role are eligible. Unverified heirs remain research targets and are not scored.</p></div><div id="pf-successors" class="pf-grid"></div></div></section>
<section class="pf-section" id="faces-operators"><div class="wrap"><div class="pf-head"><div class="eyebrow">G. Public Faces and Operators</div><h2>THE NAME ON STAGE VERSUS THE HAND ON THE MECHANISM.</h2><p>This comparison distinguishes public executive visibility from non-public capital, continuity, policy, security and appointment access.</p></div><div id="pf-faces-operators" class="pf-comparison"></div></div></section>

